{"name":"Blood God","hex":"#67080b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vital liquid flowing in the bodies of many types of animals that usually conveys nutrients and oxygen. In vertebrates, it is colored red by hemoglobin, is conveyed by arteries and veins, is pumped by the heart and is usually generated in bone marrow.","A family relationship due to birth, such as that between siblings; contrasted with relationships due to marriage or adoption. See blood relative, blood relation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause something to be covered with blood; to bloody.","To let blood (from); to bleed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blood"},{"term":"god","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Godié."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deity or supreme being; a supernatural, typically immortal, being with superior powers, to which personhood is attributed.","An idol.\nA representation of a deity, especially a statue or statuette.\n Something or someone particularly revered, worshipped, idealized, admired and/or followed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/god"}],"entries":[{"title":"Human sacrifice","blocks":[{"text":"Human sacrifice is the act of killing one or more humans as part of a ritual, which is typically intended to please or appease gods, a human ruler, public or jurisdictional demands for justice by capital punishment, an authoritative/priestly figure, spirits of dead ancestors, or as a retainer sacrifice, wherein a monarch's servants are killed in order for them to continue to serve their master in the next life. Closely related practices found in some tribal societies are cannibalism and headhunting. Human sacrifice is also known as ritual murder."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Sacrifici_d%27Ifig%C3%A8nia_%28Emp%C3%BAries%29.jpg/330px-Sacrifici_d%27Ifig%C3%A8nia_%28Emp%C3%BAries%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_sacrifice"},{"title":"Blood","blocks":[{"text":"Blood is a specialized form of connective tissue and body fluid in the circulatory system of humans and other vertebrates that delivers necessary substances such as nutrients and oxygen to the cells of the body, and transports metabolic waste products away from those same cells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg/330px-Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood"},{"title":"God","blocks":[{"text":"A supreme deity, supreme being, supreme god, or simply just God, is a deity within theistic belief systems which is believed to be the ultimate cause of all things in existence. As such, it is seen as the creator, sustainer, and ruler of the universe. God is often thought of as incorporeal and independent of the material creation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Michelangelo%2C_Creation_of_Adam_04.jpg/330px-Michelangelo%2C_Creation_of_Adam_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/God"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Le_Tour_du_monde-07-p101.jpg/500px-Le_Tour_du_monde-07-p101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Le_Tour_du_monde-07-p101.jpg/1280px-Le_Tour_du_monde-07-p101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Le_Tour_du_monde-07-p101.jpg/500px-Le_Tour_du_monde-07-p101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human sacrifice in the kingdom of Dahomey"